; pi4TftpProbe.pi4 - RaspberryPi4/Lib/tftp.pi4 walked from "does the
; codec work with no server at all" through to a file actually pulled
; onto this board over Ethernet, with every stage printing its reading
; before the next stage depends on it.
;
; DIAGNOSTIC. Does not ship.
;
;   PureMetalForge.exe --compile RaspberryPi4/Examples/Diagnostics/pi4TftpProbe.pi4 -t pi4 \
;            --load-addr 0x400000 --stack-addr 0x3000000 \
;            --entry-returns -o tftp.img
;
; --entry-returns IS NOT OPTIONAL. Without it the payload runs off its
; own end and the board hangs. Every diagnostic in this directory that
; needs it says so in its own header, because the build line is the
; thing people copy from the wrong file.
;
; ARM THE DEADMAN BEFORE RUNNING THIS: `deadman 60`. Stage 5 will sit
; for up to thirty seconds waiting for a server that may not be there,
; and a board that looks hung for thirty seconds is a board somebody
; power-cycles at second twenty-five.
;
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  IT CANNOT DAMAGE ANYTHING, AND THAT IS ON PURPOSE
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  A TFTP client writes bytes a stranger chose into memory this board
;  owns. Nothing here can hurt the hardware; it can very easily hurt the
;  BOOT IMAGE, and that costs pulling the stick out and rewriting it on
;  another machine.
;
;  SO THIS PROBE USES TftpSetSinkNone(). The file is counted and thrown
;  away. Nothing is written anywhere. That makes it the right thing to
;  run FIRST on a bench, because a wrong server address, a wrong
;  filename or a wrong anything else costs a printed line and not an
;  afternoon.
;
;  To land the bytes somewhere, change #TP_SINK to 1 and read the two
;  paragraphs beside #TP_DEST_BASE before you do. To put the file on the
;  boot medium instead, use TftpSetSinkCaller() and hand
;  TftpBlockData() / TftpBlockLen() to fat.pi4 in the pump loop - tftp.pi4
;  cannot do that itself, because a library never includes a library.
;
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  WHAT THIS IS PROVING, AND IN WHAT ORDER
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  tftp.pi4 sits on top of net.pi4, which sits on top of genet.pi4, and
;  NONE of the three does its own input or output. So this probe is the
;  pump, and the pump is the whole of the wiring:
;
;      GenetRecvWait -> NetInput -> TftpInput -> NetUdpBuild -> GenetSend
;
;  1. THE CODEC, WITH NO WIRE AND NO SERVER. A read request is built and
;     its nineteen-odd octets are printed, and then a canned DATA packet
;     held in this file as literal bytes is fed straight into
;     TftpInput() and the acknowledgement is printed. If those two are
;     right, the whole of the opcodes, the block numbering and the
;     transfer-identifier rule are proven WITHOUT A CABLE, A SWITCH OR
;     A SERVER. If they are wrong, nothing that follows is worth reading
;     and the cause is in this tree rather than out on the bench.
;
;     THE GATE tools/a64/a64_tftp_check.py DOES THIS FAR MORE
;     THOROUGHLY - 179 cases, byte-exact, twenty-one mutations. Run that
;     first. This stage exists so that a person at the bench with a
;     board that is misbehaving can see in two lines whether the problem
;     is up here or down on the wire.
;
;  2. THE WIRE. genet.pi4's four readings, briefly. pi4GenetProbe.pi4 is
;     the file for diagnosing layer 2.
;
;  3. THE ADDRESSES, printed as dotted quads so a human can compare them
;     against what they typed on the server.
;
;  4. THE READ REQUEST GOES OUT, to port 69 - and the probe prints that
;     it went to 69, because that is the one packet in a transfer that
;     does.
;
;  5. THE PUMP RUNS until the transfer completes, fails, or thirty
;     seconds pass. Every block is counted. THE SERVER'S TRANSFER
;     IDENTIFIER IS PRINTED as soon as it is known, because a client
;     that keeps talking to port 69 is the classic first-TFTP-client
;     failure and this is the line that shows it did not.
;
;  6. THE TALLY. Blocks, bytes, duplicates, gaps, strangers,
;     retransmissions - and, if it failed, the refusal in English and
;     the server's own words.
;
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  WHAT TO POINT AT IT
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  On Windows: tftpd64, with its TFTP server tab bound to the laptop's
;  address on the direct cable and its base directory holding the file.
;  On Linux:
;      sudo dnsmasq --enable-tftp --tftp-root=/srv/tftp --port=0 -d
;
;  PUT A FILE OF EXACTLY 1024 BYTES THERE AND FETCH THAT FIRST:
;      head -c 1024 /dev/urandom > /srv/tftp/exact1024.bin
;  1024 is an exact multiple of 512, so the transfer can only end on a
;  final DATA packet carrying ZERO bytes. That is the case a first TFTP
;  client gets wrong, and the one worth proving on real silicon against
;  a real server rather than only in the gate.
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------

XIncludeFile "Anvil/Hal/hal.pbi"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/uart.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/timer.pi4"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/genet.pi4"
XIncludeFile "Anvil/Network/net.pbi"
XIncludeFile "RaspberryPi4/Lib/tftp.pi4"

; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
;  THE THINGS TO CHANGE BEFORE A RUN
; ----------------------------------------------------------------------
; All addresses as four octets, so nothing here depends on knowing which
; end of a 32-bit number the first octet lives at.
#TP_IP_A = 169
#TP_IP_B = 254
#TP_IP_C = 183
#TP_IP_D = 50

#TP_MASK_A = 255
#TP_MASK_B = 255
#TP_MASK_C = 0
#TP_MASK_D = 0

#TP_GW_A = 169
#TP_GW_B = 254
#TP_GW_C = 183
#TP_GW_D = 67

; The machine running the TFTP server. On a direct cable with two
; machines on it, this is the laptop, and it is also the gateway,
; because there is nothing else to nominate.
#TP_SRV_A = 169
#TP_SRV_B = 254
#TP_SRV_C = 183
#TP_SRV_D = 67

; WHERE THE FILE GOES.
;   0 = nowhere. Counted and discarded. THE SAFE DEFAULT, and the one to
;       run first on any bench.
;   1 = memory at #TP_DEST_BASE, at most #TP_DEST_BYTES of it.
#TP_SINK = 0

; If #TP_SINK is 1, this is where the bytes land. $05000000 is in the
; low DRAM bank, above the GENET receive region at $04000000 and its
; 512 KiB, and far above both the image at $00400000 and the stack top
; at $03000000.
;
; CHECK THIS AGAINST WHAT ELSE IS IN MEMORY BEFORE YOU CHANGE IT. The
; library bounds-checks against #TP_DEST_BYTES and refuses rather than
; running past it, but it cannot know what is on the other side of the
; base address, because nothing tells it.
#TP_DEST_BASE  = $05000000
#TP_DEST_BYTES = 4194304

; The RX region genet.pi4 requires. 512 KiB - 256 descriptors of 2048
; bytes - at $04000000.
#TP_RX_REGION = $04000000
#TP_RX_BYTES  = 524288

#TP_LINK_MS = 2000         ; how long to wait for auto-negotiation
#TP_TX_MS   = 100          ; how long to wait for one frame to leave

; The pump. 250 ms per slice, 120 slices, so thirty seconds of real
; listening. A DURATION, NOT A POLL COUNT - genet.pi4's GenetRecvWait()
; header says why that distinction cost a hardware run.
#TP_SLICE_MS = 250
#TP_SLICES   = 120

; The retransmit timer handed to tftp.pi4. Two seconds and eight tries
; is sixteen seconds of patience, which fits inside the thirty above
; with room to see it give up rather than being cut off mid-way.
#TP_TIMEOUT_MS = 2000
#TP_RETRIES    = 8

Global Dim tpMac.a[6]
Global Dim tpRx.a[1600]
Global Dim tpData.a[36]        ; a canned DATA packet, byte for byte

Global tpIp.i
Global tpMask.i
Global tpGw.i
Global tpSrv.i
Global tpPort.i

Global tpFramesIn.i
Global tpUdpIn.i
Global tpSendFail.i
Global tpTidPrinted.i


Procedure PutHexN(v.i, digits.i)
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  For i = digits - 1 To 0 Step -1
    n = (v >> (i * 4)) & $F
    If n < 10
      UartWrite(48 + n)
    Else
      UartWrite(55 + n)
    EndIf
  Next
EndProcedure

Procedure Line(*name, v.i)
  UartWriteStr("  ")
  UartWriteStr(*name)
  UartWriteStr("  ")
  PrintDec(v)
  PrintNl()
EndProcedure

Procedure HexLine(*name, v.i, digits.i)
  UartWriteStr("  ")
  UartWriteStr(*name)
  UartWriteStr("  $")
  PutHexN(v, digits)
  PrintNl()
EndProcedure

; An IPv4 address the way a person writes one. net.pi4 holds an address
; with its FIRST OCTET IN THE MOST SIGNIFICANT BYTE, so this reads it
; from the top down and there is nothing to reverse.
Procedure DotLine(*name, ip.i)
  UartWriteStr("  ")
  UartWriteStr(*name)
  UartWriteStr("  ")
  PrintDec((ip >> 24) & $FF)
  UartWrite(46)                    ; ASCII full stop
  PrintDec((ip >> 16) & $FF)
  UartWrite(46)
  PrintDec((ip >> 8) & $FF)
  UartWrite(46)
  PrintDec(ip & $FF)
  PrintNl()
EndProcedure

Procedure Say(*s)
  UartWriteStr(*s)
  PrintNl()
EndProcedure

; The staged packet, as hexadecimal. A TFTP packet is small enough to
; read on a terminal and reading it is often the whole diagnosis.
Procedure ShowStaged(*name)
  Define i.i
  Define n.i
  n = TftpOutLen()
  UartWriteStr("  ")
  UartWriteStr(*name)
  UartWriteStr("  ")
  PrintDec(n)
  UartWriteStr(" octets to ")
  PrintDec((TftpOutIp() >> 24) & $FF)
  UartWrite(46)
  PrintDec((TftpOutIp() >> 16) & $FF)
  UartWrite(46)
  PrintDec((TftpOutIp() >> 8) & $FF)
  UartWrite(46)
  PrintDec(TftpOutIp() & $FF)
  UartWriteStr(" port ")
  PrintDec(TftpOutPort())
  PrintNl()
  UartWriteStr("    ")
  i = 0
  While i < n
    PutHexN(PeekA(TftpOutBuf() + i), 2)
    UartWrite(32)                  ; ASCII space
    i = i + 1
  Wend
  PrintNl()
EndProcedure

; The last tftp.pi4 refusal, in words. Kept separate from WhyNet and
; WhyGenet because the three libraries have three error variables, and
; printing the wrong one while chasing a fault costs more time than the
; three procedures cost.
Procedure WhyTftp()
  UartWriteStr("  -> ")
  UartWriteStr(TftpErrorText())
  PrintNl()
EndProcedure

Procedure WhyNet()
  UartWriteStr("  -> ")
  UartWriteStr(NetErrorText())
  PrintNl()
EndProcedure

Procedure WhyGenet()
  UartWriteStr("  -> ")
  UartWriteStr(GenetErrorText())
  PrintNl()
EndProcedure

; A canned DATA packet: opcode 3, block 1, thirty-two bytes of payload.
; Held here as literal bytes so that stage 1 can prove the receive path
; with nothing else in the room. It is SHORT - thirty-two is less than
; 512 - so it must be recognised as the final block of a one-block file.
Procedure TpLoadFrames()
  Define i.i
  tpData[0] = $00
  tpData[1] = $03                  ; opcode 3, DATA
  tpData[2] = $00
  tpData[3] = $01                  ; block 1
  For i = 0 To 31
    tpData[4 + i] = 97 + (i % 23)  ; the letters a..w, as ping sends
  Next
EndProcedure

; Send whatever tftp.pi4 has staged, through net.pi4 and genet.pi4.
; THIS IS THE WHOLE OF THE WIRING and it is four lines: read the
; destination out of tftp.pi4, wrap it in UDP, hand the frame to the
; MAC.
;
; READ TftpOutIp() AND TftpOutPort() EVERY TIME. Nearly every packet
; goes to the server and then one does not - the error sent to a
; stranger who used the wrong transfer identifier goes to the stranger.
Procedure.i TpSendStaged()
  If TftpOutLen() = 0
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  If NetUdpBuild(#HW_LINK_WIRED, TftpOutIp(), TftpOutPort(), TftpLocalPort(), TftpOutBuf(), TftpOutLen()) = 0
    WhyNet()
    tpSendFail = tpSendFail + 1
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  If GenetSend(NetOutBuf(), NetOutLen(), #TP_TX_MS) <> 1
    WhyGenet()
    tpSendFail = tpSendFail + 1
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn 1
EndProcedure

; One slice of the pump. Returns 1 if the transfer is over, either way.
Procedure.i TpPump(ms.i)
  Define n.i
  Define r.i
  Define t.i

  n = GenetRecvWait(@tpRx[0], 1600, ms)
  If n > 0
    tpFramesIn = tpFramesIn + 1
    r = NetInput(#HW_LINK_WIRED, @tpRx[0], n)
    If r = #NET_IN_REPLY
      ; An ARP request for us. Answer it - the server cannot send us a
      ; single block until it knows our hardware address.
      GenetSend(NetOutBuf(), NetOutLen(), #TP_TX_MS)
    ElseIf r = #NET_IN_UDP
      tpUdpIn = tpUdpIn + 1
      t = TftpInput(NetUdpRxFrom(), NetUdpRxPort(), NetUdpRxDstPort(), NetUdpRxData(), NetUdpRxLen())
      If tpTidPrinted = 0 And TftpTidLocked() = 1
        tpTidPrinted = 1
        Line("server TID     ", TftpServerPort())
        Say("  (that is NOT 69, and it must not be - the reply comes from")
        Say("   a new ephemeral port and everything after it goes there)")
      EndIf
      If t < 0
        Line("TftpInput      ", t)
        WhyTftp()
      ElseIf t = #TFTP_IN_STRANGER
        Say("  a stranger used the wrong transfer identifier; answering them")
      EndIf
      TpSendStaged()
    EndIf
  EndIf

  ; OUR OWN TIMER, and it is not optional. A receiver that declines to
  ; answer duplicates - which this one does, and must, or every packet
  ; doubles for the rest of the transfer - hangs forever the first time
  ; an acknowledgement is lost unless something re-sends on its own
  ; schedule. This is that something.
  t = TftpTick(millis())
  If t = 1
    Say("  timer fired - retransmitting")
    TpSendStaged()
  ElseIf t < 0
    Line("TftpTick       ", t)
    WhyTftp()
  EndIf

  If TftpComplete() = 1
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  If TftpFailed() = 1
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn 0
EndProcedure


Procedure.i Main()
  Define i.i
  Define r.i
  Define ok.i
  Define phy.i
  Define done.i

  PrintNl()
  Say("=== tftp.pi4 - RFC 1350 over UDP over IPv4 over GENET ===")
  PrintNl()

  tpMac[0] = $02
  tpMac[1] = $00
  tpMac[2] = $4D
  tpMac[3] = $46
  tpMac[4] = $00
  tpMac[5] = $01
  TpLoadFrames()
  TimerInit()
  NetInit()
  TftpInit()

  tpIp   = NetMakeIPv4(#TP_IP_A, #TP_IP_B, #TP_IP_C, #TP_IP_D)
  tpMask = NetMakeIPv4(#TP_MASK_A, #TP_MASK_B, #TP_MASK_C, #TP_MASK_D)
  tpGw   = NetMakeIPv4(#TP_GW_A, #TP_GW_B, #TP_GW_C, #TP_GW_D)
  tpSrv  = NetMakeIPv4(#TP_SRV_A, #TP_SRV_B, #TP_SRV_C, #TP_SRV_D)

  ; ==================================================================
  ;  1. THE CODEC, WITH NO WIRE AND NO SERVER
  ; ==================================================================
  Say("1. codec self-test, off the wire")
  Line("sink none      ", TftpSetSinkNone())
  Line("begin read     ", TftpBeginRead(tpSrv, "selftest.bin", 2048))
  If TftpOutLen() = 0
    WhyTftp()
    Say("  the codec is broken. Run tools/a64/a64_tftp_check.py.")
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  ShowStaged("read request ")
  Say("  (opcode 0001, then the name, a zero, 'octet', a zero)")
  Line("goes to port   ", TftpOutPort())
  If TftpOutPort() <> 69
    Say("  *** a read request must go to port 69 ***")
  EndIf

  ; Feed the canned DATA packet in as if it had arrived from port 5000.
  r = TftpInput(tpSrv, 5000, 2048, @tpData[0], 36)
  Line("canned DATA in ", r)
  If r <> #TFTP_IN_LAST
    WhyTftp()
    Say("  a 32-byte block is SHORT, so it is the last block of the file")
    Say("  and this should have been 2. Run the gate.")
  EndIf
  ShowStaged("acknowledgement")
  Line("server TID now ", TftpServerPort())
  If TftpServerPort() <> 5000
    Say("  *** the transfer identifier was not adopted from the DATA ***")
  EndIf
  Line("bytes          ", TftpBytes())
  PrintNl()

  ; ==================================================================
  ;  2. THE WIRE
  ; ==================================================================
  Say("2. the wire")
  ok = GenetProbe()
  HexLine("SYS_REV_CTRL   ", GenetRevision(), 8)
  Line("probe ok       ", ok)
  If ok <> 1
    WhyGenet()
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  phy = GenetPhyScan()
  Line("PHY address    ", phy)
  If phy < 0
    WhyGenet()
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  ok = GenetPhyWaitLink(#TP_LINK_MS)
  Line("link up        ", ok)
  If ok <> 1
    WhyGenet()
    Say("  no link. Check the cable is in, at both ends.")
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  If GenetPhyResolve() = 1
    Line("speed Mbit/s   ", GenetSpeed())
    Line("full duplex    ", GenetFullDuplex())
  EndIf
  Line("set mac        ", GenetSetMac(@tpMac[0]))
  Line("set rx region  ", GenetSetRxRegion(#TP_RX_REGION, #TP_RX_BYTES))
  ok = GenetStart(#TP_LINK_MS)
  Line("genet start    ", ok)
  If ok <> 1
    WhyGenet()
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  PrintNl()

  ; ==================================================================
  ;  3. THE ADDRESSES
  ; ==================================================================
  Say("3. addresses")
  NetInit()
  Line("set mac        ", NetSetMac(#HW_LINK_WIRED, @tpMac[0]))
  ok = NetSetIPv4(#HW_LINK_WIRED, tpIp, tpMask, tpGw)
  Line("set addresses  ", ok)
  If ok <> 1
    WhyNet()
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  DotLine("board          ", NetIPv4(#HW_LINK_WIRED))
  DotLine("netmask        ", NetMask(#HW_LINK_WIRED))
  DotLine("gateway        ", NetGateway(#HW_LINK_WIRED))
  DotLine("tftp server    ", tpSrv)
  PrintNl()

  ; ==================================================================
  ;  4. THE READ REQUEST
  ; ==================================================================
  Say("4. the read request")
  TftpInit()
  If #TP_SINK = 1
    Line("sink memory    ", TftpSetMemory(#TP_DEST_BASE, #TP_DEST_BYTES))
    HexLine("destination    ", #TP_DEST_BASE, 8)
    Line("capacity bytes ", #TP_DEST_BYTES)
  Else
    Line("sink none      ", TftpSetSinkNone())
    Say("  (the file is counted and discarded. Nothing is written.)")
  EndIf
  Line("timer ms       ", #TP_TIMEOUT_MS)
  Line("retries        ", TftpSetTimeout(#TP_TIMEOUT_MS, #TP_RETRIES))

  ; Our own transfer identifier. U-Boot's arithmetic on a seed we have:
  ; the millisecond clock. [v2025.01_net_tftp.c:924]
  tpPort = TftpSuggestPort(millis())
  Line("our TID        ", tpPort)
  Line("udp bind       ", NetUdpBind(#HW_LINK_WIRED, tpPort))

  ok = TftpBeginRead(tpSrv, "exact1024.bin", tpPort)
  Line("begin read     ", ok)
  If ok <> 1
    WhyTftp()
    ProcedureReturn 1
  EndIf
  ShowStaged("read request ")
  Line("sent           ", TpSendStaged())
  PrintNl()

  ; ==================================================================
  ;  5. THE PUMP
  ; ==================================================================
  Say("5. pumping, up to thirty seconds")
  done = 0
  For i = 1 To #TP_SLICES
    If TpPump(#TP_SLICE_MS) = 1
      done = 1
      Break
    EndIf
  Next
  If done = 0
    Say("  thirty seconds passed and the transfer neither finished nor")
    Say("  failed. That means nothing came back at all - check that the")
    Say("  server is running, that its address is the one printed in")
    Say("  stage 3, and that it is serving the filename asked for.")
  EndIf
  PrintNl()

  ; ==================================================================
  ;  6. THE TALLY
  ; ==================================================================
  Say("6. the tally")
  Line("frames in      ", tpFramesIn)
  Line("datagrams in   ", tpUdpIn)
  Line("blocks         ", TftpBlocksDone())
  Line("bytes          ", TftpBytes())
  Line("wraps          ", TftpWraps())
  Line("duplicates     ", TftpDupCount())
  Line("gaps           ", TftpGapCount())
  Line("strangers      ", TftpStrangerCount())
  Line("retransmits    ", TftpRetransmitCount())
  Line("ignored        ", TftpIgnoredCount())
  Line("send failures  ", tpSendFail)
  Line("server TID     ", TftpServerPort())
  UartWriteStr("  state          ")
  UartWriteStr(TftpStateText())
  PrintNl()

  If TftpComplete() = 1
    Say("  COMPLETE.")
    If #TP_SINK = 1
      Say("  The file is in memory at the destination printed in stage 4.")
    Else
      Say("  Nothing was written, by design. Set #TP_SINK to 1 to land it.")
    EndIf
    ProcedureReturn 0
  EndIf

  WhyTftp()
  If TftpServerCode() <> 0 Or TftpServerMessageLen() > 0
    UartWriteStr("  the server said  ")
    UartWriteStr(TftpCodeText(TftpServerCode()))
    PrintNl()
    UartWriteStr("  in its own words ")
    UartWriteStr(TftpServerMessage())
    PrintNl()
    Line("worth retrying ", TftpRetryWorthwhile())
  EndIf
  ProcedureReturn 1
EndProcedure
